        "operation": "A local query selects a node $i$ and a point $x\\in\\mathbb R^d$ and returns $G_i(x;\\xi)$ satisfying $\\mathbb E[G_i\\mid\\mathcal F]=\\nabla f_i(x)$ and $\\mathbb E[\\|G_i-\\nabla f_i(x)\\|^2\\mid\\mathcal F]\\le\\sigma^2$ for the complete pre-query history $\\mathcal F$. Every call uses fresh randomness. No same-sample second-point reuse or smoothness of random responses is provided. Function values are not returned. One communication call applies W to any finite stack of local vectors. Exact real local arithmetic is unrestricted and may use the known matrix, signed coefficients, and public randomness. Communication calls are counted separately but are not capped when the total sample count is optimized.",
